<p>
Seed for red-osier dogwood and thin-leaf alder were collected near the project site last year and grown in the greenhouse this summer.  The quaking aspen and serviceberry plants were grown from seed collected at a 4,000 foot elevation site near McCall, Idaho; a close and similar habitat to the Red River meadow.  Quaking aspen seed was not found on our site last year.  Serviceberry and hawthorn seed sources were found on site but proved unproductive.  We'll keep trying! 
